<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  One destination in the navigation rail. Inflated by BrowseActivity rather than <include>d
  repeatedly, because each copy needs its own icon and label and <include> cannot supply either.

  Focusable in its own right - unlike the app grid's cells, this is a plain view in a plain
  LinearLayout, so android:stateListAnimator works here and the framework moves focus between
  items with no help.

  The icon sits in a column exactly as wide as the collapsed rail's content area, and this view
  has NO horizontal padding of its own. Both halves are load-bearing, and each was got wrong once:

    - Padding cannot centre the icon. Symmetric 24dp either side of a 32dp icon needs 80dp inside
      a rail that offers 72dp, so every icon lost its right-hand edge.

    - Padding cannot survive alongside the column either, even once the icon is centred by the
      column instead. ViewGroup.clipToPadding defaults to TRUE, so a paddingEnd here clips the
      children to the content box - and the column is deliberately the FULL item width, so the
      last 24dp of it got sliced off. That cost the "add" disc a visible chord while leaving the
      gear, whose rightmost ink is a shallow tooth, looking fine: the same bug, visible on one
      icon and not the other.

  So the trailing space for the label lives on the label, as a margin. If horizontal padding is
  ever added back here, rail_icon_column has to shrink by the same amount or the clipping returns.

  Sizing the column this way also has the side benefit that the icons do not shift when the rail
  expands - only the labels arrive.

  The focus animator is rail-specific: a match_parent row cannot be scaled the way a tile can.
  See rail_item_focus.xml.

  The label is present at all widths and simply clipped while the rail is collapsed. Animating a
  width the text is already laid out for is what lets ChangeBounds do the whole expansion; adding
  and removing the TextView instead would re-measure the text on every focus change.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="@dimen/rail_item_height"
    android:orientation="horizontal"
    android:gravity="center_vertical"
    android:layout_marginBottom="@dimen/space_2"
    android:background="@drawable/rail_item_background"
    android:stateListAnimator="@animator/rail_item_focus"
    android:focusable="true"
    android:clickable="true">

    <ImageView
        android:id="@+id/railIcon"
        android:importantForAccessibility="no"
        android:layout_width="@dimen/rail_icon_column"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/rail_icon_size"
        android:scaleType="fitCenter" />

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/railLabel"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_2"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/space_5"
        android:singleLine="true"
        android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Moonlight.Rail" />

</LinearLayout>
